#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0350 expect=noViolation domain=DM
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when --SCAT is equal to the domain name.
#note "DMSCAT is populated and NOT equal to the DM label 'Demographics' -> no violation. Fix #371: the library MUST be wired here — before it, this scenario passed VACUOUSLY (no library ⇒ the label was never read ⇒ the not-empty guard silenced the rule), so it proved nothing about the comparison."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#library dataset-metadata DM label=Demographics
dataset DM label=Demographics
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DMSCAT type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 | BASELINE
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023 | BASELINE
---
